|~ The verbs of maps [D62]. Each resides on `::qlang/map`, the kind whose
   module declares it, under the contract of its name on `::qlang/any`,
   whose page and laws it answers [D72]. A map's elements are its
   values, and its keys are the shape that travels with them [D15]: a
   verb that keeps the kind keeps the keys of the entries it keeps. ~|

:count
  |~~ The number of entries.

      ~({:x 1 :y 2 :z 3} | count | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::number | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/count})

:empty
  |~~ Whether the map holds no entry.

      ~({} | empty | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/empty})

:first
  |~~ The value of the first entry, or null for the empty map.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | first | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/first})

:last
  |~~ The value of the last entry, or null for the empty map.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | last | eq 2)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/last})

:sum
  |~~ The sum of the values, each a number.

      ~({:a 10 :b 20} | sum | eq 30)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::number | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/sum})

:min
  |~~ The first value in the one order of values.

      ~({:a 3 :b 1} | min | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/min})

:max
  |~~ The last value in the one order of values.

      ~({:a 3 :b 1} | max | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/max})

:filter
  |~~ The entries whose value the predicate answers true for, their keys
      kept; the joint test of a key with its value reads the keys, `m |
      keys | filter ~(…)`, and `at` the value of each.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | filter ~(gt 1) | eq {:b 2 :c 3})
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:predicate ::quote | :returns / | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/filter})

:every
  |~~ Whether the predicate answers true for every value.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | every ~(gt 0) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:predicate ::quote | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/every})

:any
  |~~ Whether the predicate answers true for some value.

      ~({:a -1 :b 0 :c 2} | any ~(gt 0) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:predicate ::quote | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/any})

:sort
  |~~ The entries ordered by their values, or by the value the key
      answers for each, their keys kept.

      ~({:a 3 :b 1 :c 2} | sort | vals | eq [1 2 3])
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:key #[::quote ::null] | :returns / | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/sort})

:take
  |~~ The first count entries.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | take 2 | eq {:a 1 :b 2})
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:count ::number | :returns / | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/take})

:drop
  |~~ The entries after the first count.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | drop 2 | eq {:c 3})
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:count ::number | :returns / | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/drop})

:at
  |~~ The value at the key, a keyword or a string, both naming the key
      as the map stores it, or null for a key the map lacks: the soft
      counterpart of the strict `/key` projection, which refuses a
      miss with `::ProjectionKeyNotInMapError`.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | at :a | eq 1)
      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | at "a" | eq 1)
      ~({:a 1} | at :z | eq null)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:key #[::keyword ::string] | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/at})

::AtKeyNotKeywordOrStringError
  |~~ The key of `at` on a map is a keyword or a string, both naming the
      key as the map stores it.

      ~(
        {:a 1} | at 42
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AtKeyNotKeywordOrStringError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:reverse
  |~~ The entries in the reverse order, their keys kept.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | reverse | vals | eq [2 1])
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns / | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/reverse})

:reduce
  |~~ The seed folded over the values by the reducer.

      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | reduce 0 ~(add) | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:seed ::any | :reducer ::quote | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/reduce})
